1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,350
Read

2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,350
Are you really breaking things off?

3
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:03,350
Come on, lighten up.

4
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,350
Read

5
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,900
<i>I don't get it.</i>

6
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,590
<i>Why's this happening?</i>

7
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:11,600
<i>Clearly, she wasn't happy about 
Enomoto-san becoming the main model.</i>

8
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:12,990
<i>But why?</i>

9
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:18,690
<i>This is starting to piss me off!</i>

10
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:41,930
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

11
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:41,930
(No, It Can't!!)

12
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:54,000
Hydrangea and a New Seed

13
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:07,480
<i>"Can't stop thinking about cute old me 
now that we're not speaking?"</i>

14
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,980
<i>"You like me way too much, Yu!"</i>

15
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:11,010
<i>Or something like that.</i>

16
00:02:11,510 --> 00:02:13,010
<i>Sure, she's cute.</i>

17
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:16,210
<i>But you know what? 
What comes around goes around.</i>

18
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:18,960
<i>If that's how it is, then...</i>

19
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:29,550
Man, spice and Yoghurppe
 go together in such sweet harmony!

20
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:32,460
But I dunno if I can eat all this by myself.

21
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:34,960
If only there were someone to share it with.

22
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:39,570
So? What's bothering you?

23
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:43,050
<i>She's actually planning to ignore me!</i>

24
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:44,490
Fine then.

25
00:02:44,730 --> 00:02:47,520
I guess we're not opening 
a store together after all.

26
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,850
Did you hear that?

27
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,970
What a dick move.

28
00:02:57,970 --> 00:03:00,330
Whatever's going on, 
she didn't deserve that.

29
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,640
<i>Damn that Himari magic!</i>

30
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:05,580
<i>This just looks like I'm bullying her.</i>

31
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,170
Himari

32
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,170
Ms. Himari Inuzuka
 Talent Agency Origin Production

33
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,780
<i>Himari forwarded me an email?</i>

34
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,590
<i>"Thank you for joining our agency.</i>

35
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,370
<i>In preparation for your transfer 
to Tokyo by the end of May,</i>

36
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:24,560
<i>we would like to visit your parents..."</i>

37
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:25,160
No way!

38
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,310
You're joining a talent agency?

39
00:03:29,890 --> 00:03:31,180
Bwa-ha!

40
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:31,720
<i>Wha?!</i>

41
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,250
<i>She got me!</i>

42
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,180
Hold up, Himari!

43
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,330
Dammit, she got away.

44
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:43,860
Yu-kun!

45
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:47,260
Hii-chan sent me this a second ago.

46
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,500
<i>I'm going to Tokyo, so have fun with Yu!</i>

47
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,560
Seriously?

48
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,510
I'm sorry, Yu-kun.

49
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,260
This all happened because I wanted to model.

50
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,800
No, it's not your fault at all.

51
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,840
We just need to find her and talk it out.

52
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,050
Here, I have just the thing.

53
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:06,510
Nice, homemade cookies!

54
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:09,560
That reminds me, I have her favorite drink.

55
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,190
I hope Hii-chan comes...

56
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:18,830
No way she can resist your awesome cookies.

57
00:04:18,830 --> 00:04:19,850
I guarantee it'll work!

58
00:04:19,850 --> 00:04:21,410
You two!

59
00:04:21,410 --> 00:04:25,960
Don't think you can lure me 
with sweets that easily!

60
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,320
I can see you hiding!

61
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:28,840
Hey!

62
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,990
Bam! Gotcha!

63
00:04:30,990 --> 00:04:33,420
See, I knew you'd show up!

64
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:36,200
<i>What an idiot.</i>

65
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:39,460
Himari! Just hear me out.

66
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,810
Sh-Shut up!

67
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:42,130
I have nothing to talk to you about!

68
00:04:42,130 --> 00:04:45,760
Liar! You've basically 
been begging for attention!

69
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,960
No, I haven't!

70
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:49,480
Himari!

71
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:51,150
Yu-kun!

72
00:04:51,150 --> 00:04:52,100
Wait up! Himari!

73
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:54,140
I said leave me alone!

74
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,050
What are you so upset about?

75
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:03,440
You're that mad about Enomoto-san modeling?

76
00:05:04,770 --> 00:05:06,240
It's not about Enocchi!

77
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,580
<i>You're</i> the one who's pissing me off!

78
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,700
What? You can't be serious!

79
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:17,670
Science Room

80
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,130
How's it fair that I get juice poured on me?

81
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:16,220
Or that the entire class thinks I'm a dick?

82
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:17,670
Or that I get slapped out of nowhere?

83
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,180
Now you're going to Tokyo?

84
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:23,420
You could've at least talked to me about it.

85
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,400
Shows how little I mattered to you.

86
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:31,010
Was I just some toy for you to tease 
and play with all this time?

87
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:34,590
Don't just stand there! Say something!

88
00:05:34,590 --> 00:05:35,720
Stop!

89
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,680
Calm down!

90
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,600
I <i>am</i> calm!

91
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,060
Just let me go!

92
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:41,880
Listen to what I'm saying!

93
00:05:47,110 --> 00:05:47,820
Sorry!

94
00:05:49,290 --> 00:05:50,120
Move!

95
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:55,000
No way... It can't be...

96
00:05:58,920 --> 00:05:59,920
Whatever.

97
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,760
I was just someone you could boss around.

98
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:06,630
Someone that made you accessories. Right?

99
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:13,930
I could say the same about you.

100
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:20,310
You only think of me as a convenient helper.

101
00:06:20,310 --> 00:06:22,240
What? I don't thinkâ€”

102
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,000
You don't?

103
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:26,310
Then why would you make 
Enocchi your main model?

104
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:32,490
Why would you give someone else 
the right to wear your accessories first?

105
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:36,460
You promised that role would be mine.

106
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:39,680
You like Enocchi, don't you?

107
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,550
That's why you're making 
her your number one.

108
00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:47,280
I get it. I know what love is.

109
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:49,240
I found out what it means.

110
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:52,460
I want to be happy for you two.

111
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:56,050
But... But...

112
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:00,280
There's no way I can be 
happy as your second choice!

113
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:07,150
I'm going where there's 
people who actually need me.

114
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:17,200
What are you doing out here?

115
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,720
Can you leave me alone?

116
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:22,080
I'm afraid not, buddy!

117
00:07:22,530 --> 00:07:25,030
Rin-chan asked me to come check on you.

118
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:28,880
Why did you ask me to make 
Enomoto-san the main model?

119
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:33,050
'Cause that seemed like the only 
way she would stand a chance.

120
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:38,480
I can see why you'd root for her, 
but that has nothing to do with modeling.

121
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:40,560
You really believe that?

122
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:47,000
The tricky thing about romance isn't 
getting together, it's staying together.

123
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,070
What's the point if it'll fall apart?

124
00:07:49,690 --> 00:07:52,340
That's especially 
convincing coming from you.

125
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,730
What a shame if you and Rin-chan 
begin dating, only for you to

126
00:07:55,730 --> 00:08:00,530
parade around with Himari-chan 
and make her the third wheel.

127
00:08:00,910 --> 00:08:03,550
But Himari and I are best friends...

128
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:08,670
Then what's with all the agony?

129
00:08:10,170 --> 00:08:13,340
"Like" and "love" aren't all that different.

130
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:17,450
Kind of like your new 
feelings towards Himari-chan.

131
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:23,380
Otherwise, you'd have no reason 
to avoid dating Rin-chan.

132
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:28,020
What's tripping you up is your guilt 
from being attracted to Himari-chan.

133
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:33,170
It's time you put aside "romance" 
or "friendship" or any of that.

134
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:37,780
What actually matters is that you 
decide who's most important to you.

135
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:41,190
I'll admit, the whole 
modeling thing with Rin-chan

136
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:45,030
was meant to tear you and Himari-chan apart.

137
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:46,540
But...

138
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:49,000
Himari-chan's decision to go 
to Tokyo shows that

139
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:54,120
she could only move on from 
you by leaving everything behind.

140
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:58,640
Who would've known she 
had such strong feelings?

141
00:09:00,570 --> 00:09:04,850
If Himari-chan actually leaves this way, 
Rin-chan would blame herself.

142
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:08,440
I don't want my childhood friend 
to go through that.

143
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:13,320
I'm not typically one to be so loyal.

144
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,530
You're actually a pretty nice person.

145
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,200
What?

146
00:09:19,050 --> 00:09:20,860
N-No, I'm not!

147
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:22,260
Stop joking around.

148
00:09:26,390 --> 00:09:30,510
You could forget Himari-chan and 
just get with Rin-chan, you know.

149
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:33,280
Whatever, do what you want.

150
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:38,240
Let me remind you that Rin-chan would 
make the best girlfriend you could find.

151
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:41,290
See, you're too nice.

152
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:48,520
<i>You knew that if you put it like that, 
I'd stop Himari from leaving.</i>

153
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,700
<i>Are you seriously going to Tokyo?</i>

154
00:10:02,970 --> 00:10:03,530
<i>Yup.</i>

155
00:10:04,110 --> 00:10:05,000
<i>Why?</i>

156
00:10:05,590 --> 00:10:07,450
<i>So I can see my own worth.</i>

157
00:10:07,970 --> 00:10:09,260
<i>See your worth...</i>

158
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,260
<i>Still as philosophical as ever, I see.</i>

159
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:15,700
<i>I doubt you'd understand.</i>

160
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,430
<i>Of course I do.</i>

161
00:10:18,250 --> 00:10:21,640
<i>I've made accessories alone all these years.</i>

162
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:26,250
<i>No one understood me. Or even cared.</i>

163
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,090
<i>I wasn't needed by anyone.</i>

164
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:33,200
<i>But thanks to Himari, 
my accessory-making career survived.</i>

165
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,880
<i>And they spread to others in the world.</i>

166
00:10:35,190 --> 00:10:39,240
<i>So I promised to keep 
making them for Himari.</i>

167
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:43,680
<i>If I turned my back on that promise, 
it's only natural she leaves.</i>

168
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,560
<i>Can we scratch going to Tokyo?</i>

169
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:47,920
<i>Nope.</i>

170
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:50,850
<i>I'll bow down and apologize 
about the modeling thing.</i>

171
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:55,490
<i>I know how stubborn Himari is.</i>

172
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:59,910
<i>She'll probably go to Tokyo 
and become popular.</i>

173
00:11:00,590 --> 00:11:02,930
<i>Whether I'm with her or not.</i>

174
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:07,110
<i>I guess it can't be helped.</i>

175
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:08,590
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

176
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,920
<i>Life doesn't always go your way.</i>

177
00:11:12,470 --> 00:11:14,440
<i>And when it doesn't...</i>

178
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,560
<i>It's up to me to make my dream come true.</i>

179
00:11:19,430 --> 00:11:20,730
<i>Bwa-ha!</i>

180
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:22,740
<i>Yu's such an idiot!</i>

181
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,940
<i>Like I'd ever go to Tokyo.</i>

182
00:11:24,940 --> 00:11:27,500
<i>I'm not so desperate that I need to</i>

183
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,360
<i>satisfy my needs through 
a bunch of strangers!</i>

184
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:33,920
<i>Well, my fake crying must have worked.</i>

185
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,580
<i>Yup, it was totally fake crying.</i>

186
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,390
<i>Why would I cry for real?</i>

187
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:43,000
<i>Yu's accessory broke, that's all.</i>

188
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,440
<i>Stop moping around!</i>

189
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:57,520
<i>You can get him to make you a new one!</i>

190
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,320
<i>I'll have him going, "Please, Himari-sama!"</i>

191
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,240
<i>And make him do whatever I want!</i>

192
00:12:05,810 --> 00:12:09,240
<i>First, a monthly event called 
"Thank you Himari-sama Day."</i>

193
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:12,350
<i>Second, he'll make me flower accessories!</i>

194
00:12:12,350 --> 00:12:15,400
<i>And third, a kissing practice system.</i>

195
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,160
<i>Next time I ask for a practice kiss,</i>

196
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:19,210
<i>he can't refuse, no matter what!</i>

197
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:22,380
<i>I feel like I'm getting 
off-topic, but oh well!</i>

198
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:25,800
<i>Tomorrow, Yu will bow down 
and apologize to me.</i>

199
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:34,720
<i>Um?</i>

200
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,240
<i>Hello?</i>

201
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:42,770
<i>Why isn't he initiating?</i>

202
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:47,550
<i>Does he need time to cry 
his eyes out from losing me?</i>

203
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:49,750
<i>Fine. Since you're cute,</i>

204
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:50,480
<i>I forgive you!</i>

205
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,560
Hello, Sensei?

206
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:58,000
<i>If I were to guess...</i>

207
00:12:58,370 --> 00:13:01,370
<i>Yu will come crying to me over the weekend!</i>

208
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:02,400
<i>I know it!</i>

209
00:13:07,590 --> 00:13:08,880
<i>Okay, I get it.</i>

210
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:13,270
<i>He must've been really upset 
about the Tokyo thing.</i>

211
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:14,890
<i>Fine! Forgiven!</i>

212
00:13:15,850 --> 00:13:17,100
<i>U-Um...</i>

213
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:20,620
<i>Maybe I'll peek 
at his socials, just in case.</i>

214
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:21,320
<i>Huh?</i>

215
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:25,420
<i>That's Yu's hand.</i>

216
00:13:28,770 --> 00:13:31,410
<i>It's like I actually 
don't belong here anymore.</i>

217
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:34,370
<i>The new product launched already, too.</i>

218
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:37,990
<i>What if I really went to Tokyo?</i>

219
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:42,640
When you do stuff like that, 
it's kind of a drag.

220
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,990
<i>Wake up, Himari!</i>

221
00:13:46,990 --> 00:13:48,860
<i>You've already been dumped, remember?</i>

222
00:13:48,860 --> 00:13:50,440
<i>There's no way he'd ask you to stay!</i>

223
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,710
Hey, Himari. Home already?

224
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:01,110
Yup! Gotta study for exams!

225
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:03,320
Wow, you're working hard.

226
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:06,540
There's some curry on the 
stove if you want some.

227
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:07,290
Okay!

228
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,480
Himari?

229
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:11,430
Hmm?

230
00:14:11,910 --> 00:14:15,630
I see you haven't spoken 
to Yu-kun in over a week.

231
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,990
Wanna fill me in?

232
00:14:20,410 --> 00:14:21,920
You're wondering how I know.

233
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:24,040
It's very simple.

234
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:28,610
I can sense your "Yu-kun aura" 
is rapidly declining.

235
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:30,510
So?

236
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,110
What happened?

237
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:35,730
You unbelievable dimwit!

238
00:14:36,070 --> 00:14:37,910
You got dumped so you 
threatened to move to Tokyo?

239
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:40,440
And now you're planning 
on ordering him around?

240
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:42,180
That's called emotional blackmail!

241
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,990
You should be ashamed to be 
a member of the Inuzuka family!

242
00:14:44,990 --> 00:14:47,160
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!
I'm sorry!

243
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:50,000
Himari, we have a deal, remember?

244
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:55,120
During that bazaar in middle school, 
you begged me for a lifetime favor.

245
00:14:55,300 --> 00:15:00,330
So to sell out 200 accessories, 
I asked Enomoto to advertise them...

246
00:15:00,330 --> 00:15:04,460
You made me beg Enomoto for help!

247
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:08,890
She forced me to bow down to her, 
lick her heels, and sing in front of her!

248
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:13,190
I haven't even endured that 
kind of humiliation at my job!

249
00:15:13,190 --> 00:15:17,720
I-I get that you despise 
Enocchi's big sister to death.

250
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,280
But I decided to help! Why?

251
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:23,340
Because his work spoke to me!

252
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,480
You remember our deal, right?

253
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:29,920
To never quit supporting Yu's 
dream to open his own store.

254
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,660
Right you are!

255
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:34,300
Don't tell me that all this time...

256
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:38,830
You were only in it for fun and were 
planning to abandon it when you got bored?

257
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:41,880
No, I swear! It's not like that!

258
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,510
Then what's this disaster about?

259
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:47,720
'C-Cause... I ended up falling for Yu!

260
00:15:49,380 --> 00:15:51,650
Onii-chan, you don't get it at all!

261
00:15:51,650 --> 00:15:53,520
What about <i>my</i> feelings?

262
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,880
I'm supposed to sacrifice myself?

263
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,580
That's right.

264
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:02,640
What's most important to you?

265
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:07,250
Is it romance? Or is it 
having Yu-kun for yourself?

266
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:09,550
Aren't they the same?

267
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,920
Everything in life is finite.

268
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:14,000
You could have all the money in the world,

269
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:18,530
but that won't get you everything you want.

270
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:23,320
As a civil servant, 
I worked on building highways.

271
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:27,590
That meant demolishing people's 
homes and taking their land.

272
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:30,510
I've been met with more 
criticism than gratitude.

273
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:31,960
But...

274
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,910
It was necessary for this town 
to survive the next 100 years.

275
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:40,800
I'm doing work that will serve a purpose, 
even after I die one day.

276
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,760
That's the kind of life I want for you, too.

277
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,040
Throw out the small stuff.

278
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:50,490
Work to grasp that one thing 
that's important to you.

279
00:16:50,970 --> 00:16:52,850
If you do that, you've won in life.

280
00:16:56,930 --> 00:17:00,080
<i>I couldn't fully understand 
Onii-chan's point.</i>

281
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:05,560
<i>But I can't throw it all away now.</i>

282
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,410
<i>Not until I understand it but can't accept it.</i>

283
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:13,760
<i>Yu, can we talk?</i>

284
00:17:14,110 --> 00:17:15,210
<i>It's important.</i>

285
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,880
<i>I have something to tell you, too.</i>

286
00:17:17,430 --> 00:17:18,610
<i>Meet me in the science room.</i>

287
00:17:20,770 --> 00:17:23,190
It's not like a super big deal.

288
00:17:23,190 --> 00:17:27,640
About that agency, it's well... um...

289
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,070
<i>Ugh! I can't figure out what I wanna say!</i>

290
00:17:31,570 --> 00:17:34,010
A-Actually, could you go first?

291
00:17:34,010 --> 00:17:35,580
I'll talk after you!

292
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:36,890
Oh, okay.

293
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:41,090
There's something I wanted to give you.

294
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,290
Notice of Withdrawal
 From School

295
00:17:46,270 --> 00:17:47,680
W-Withdrawal?!

296
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,330
Oh shit! Wrong one!

297
00:17:49,790 --> 00:17:51,960
Sorry, that's not it! I messed up!

298
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:54,410
Hang on! Forget the mistake!

299
00:17:54,410 --> 00:17:56,320
What's that notice for?

300
00:17:57,190 --> 00:17:59,700
I'm thinking of quitting school.

301
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,140
I'll go to Tokyo. I'm coming with you.

302
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:06,600
Huh? W-With me?

303
00:18:07,650 --> 00:18:11,830
Makishima told me to decide 
what's most important to me.

304
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,940
And I decided it's you.

305
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:21,340
I'd need to figure out how 
to make a living but...

306
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,400
Y-You mean... Wait.

307
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:28,300
You make it sound easy, 
but if you start working,

308
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:30,930
you won't have as much time 
to make accessories.

309
00:18:31,780 --> 00:18:35,960
No flower accessory 
is good enough without you!

310
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:42,320
But Himari, am I worth being 
with if I can't make accessories?

311
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,400
<i>Sure you are.</i>

312
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,040
<i>You're plenty!</i>

313
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:49,600
<i>I love watching videos together.</i>

314
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:53,240
<i>I love fighting over onion rings 
on the way home from school.</i>

315
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,370
<i>I love going out together 
on the train somewhere.</i>

316
00:18:57,390 --> 00:19:00,960
<i>I love every minute I get to laugh with you!</i>

317
00:19:03,070 --> 00:19:04,820
Hey! What's that for?

318
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:07,470
Don't worry. I'm not going.

319
00:19:07,760 --> 00:19:13,080
What? But you said you 
want to feel needed by fans!

320
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,030
Y-You okay?

321
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,430
I did not say that!

322
00:19:18,430 --> 00:19:20,380
And you're way too close!

323
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,920
<i>Having your face so close makes me 
want to go in for a kiss!</i>

324
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,640
<i>But I can't have my first 
kiss be all sticky with juice!</i>

325
00:19:29,550 --> 00:19:31,880
You and I can go back to normal.

326
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,680
And I don't mind Enocchi modeling.

327
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:37,640
But could you keep me
 as the... main model?

328
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:39,610
Sure.

329
00:19:39,890 --> 00:19:42,320
So what did you wanna give me?

330
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:44,530
Wow...

331
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:47,740
Is this <i>Anemone flaccida</i>? It's so small.

332
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:51,120
I made it with a preserved <i>Anemone flaccida</i>.

333
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:52,580
A mini version.

334
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:56,090
A totally unique best 
friend ring just for you.

335
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:01,720
I realized that you're my best friend.

336
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:05,100
I might make you mad again...

337
00:20:05,610 --> 00:20:08,760
But it's not like other people 
are more important than you.

338
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:10,980
I promise, that's the truth.

339
00:20:13,610 --> 00:20:15,540
Yu, turn around for a sec.

340
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:16,840
Why?

341
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:18,010
Just do it!

342
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,060
Woot!

343
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:21,570
Hey! What are you doing?

344
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:23,010
Put it on for me?

345
00:20:24,410 --> 00:20:25,680
Do it yourself.

346
00:20:26,450 --> 00:20:29,120
No! I want you to do it!

347
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,470
Boo! Loser!

348
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:35,220
I told you, it's a best friend ring.

349
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,290
Bwa-ha!

350
00:20:36,450 --> 00:20:38,290
Hey, what's this tiny thing?

351
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,760
It's an... <i>Anemone flaccida</i> seed.

352
00:20:41,470 --> 00:20:42,610
Cool!

353
00:20:42,890 --> 00:20:44,030
H-Hey.

354
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,400
You should just pick me.

355
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:52,940
If we're still alone at thirty, pick me.

356
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:56,400
Maybe, if I'm single then.

357
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:01,150
<i>In the end, things are still the same.</i>

358
00:21:01,150 --> 00:21:02,110
<i>But oh well.</i>

359
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:05,610
<i>If that's what Yu wants, 
I can stay best friends.</i>

360
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:09,770
<i>I'll keep my feelings hidden in this ring.</i>

361
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:11,720
Hey, Himari-san!

362
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:13,600
What's up?

363
00:21:13,750 --> 00:21:18,590
Is it true that this is that 
Natsume-kun you always hang out with?

364
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:25,010
How did it go?

365
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,390
<i>Oh yeah. I haven't thanked her.</i>

366
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:31,110
<i>Thanks to you, it turned 
out great. Thank you.</i>

367
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,560
<i>Glad I could help.</i>

368
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:37,300
<i>It took me some time to find it, though.</i>

369
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:42,290
<i>Pretty suave of you to sneak 
in a purple tulip seed.</i>

370
00:21:42,650 --> 00:21:44,680
<i>I bet Inuzuka-chan loved it.</i>

371
00:21:45,330 --> 00:21:47,240
<i>How did she figure that out?</i>

372
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:52,070
<i>I can't tell Himari the meaning 
behind purple tulips yet.</i>

373
00:21:52,990 --> 00:21:55,630
<i>I'd die if I got dumped back there.</i>

374
00:21:56,970 --> 00:21:58,960
<i>Someday, I'll tell her.</i>

375
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:04,560
<i>My best friend is too cute to handle.</i>

376
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:39,980
A Hunk and Morning Glory Yutaka

